---
import { Badge, Icon, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const commands = [
  { name: 'Refresh Dependency Signals', description: 'Re-analyze visible manifests.' },
  { name: 'Clear Registry Cache', description: 'Clear cached npm metadata and refresh dependency information.' },
  { name: 'Toggle Prerelease Versions', description: 'Include or exclude prerelease versions in update targets.' },
  { name: 'Sort Current Manifest', description: 'Alphabetize package sections in package.json.' },
  { name: 'Run Package Install', description: 'Start the selected package manager’s dependency install from VS Code.' },
  { name: 'Show Debug Output', description: 'Inspect activation, refresh, cache, parse, analysis, and diagnostic details in the output channel.' }
]
---

<Docs title="VS Code Extension" description="VS Code features provided by Dep Beacon.">
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow"><span>02</span> / Editor guide</p>
    <h1>Stay on the line.<br />Work in VS Code.</h1>
    <p class="docs-intro">
      Version signals, CodeLens actions, and dependency details live beside the manifest entries you are already
        editing.
    </p>
    <dl class="docs-facts">
      <div><dt>Actions</dt><dd>CodeLens + quick fixes</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Context</dt><dd>Hovers + inline labels</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <figure class="docs-media">
    <img
      src="/usage-preview.png"
      alt="Dep Beacon showing package.json and pnpm-workspace.yaml with inline version status, CodeLens update actions, and diagnostics."
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
      width="1600"
      height="900"
    />
    <figcaption>One workspace, connected signals. Package manifests and pnpm catalogs share the same dependency
      intelligence.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section aria-labelledby="update-targets">
    <h2 id="update-targets">Choose your next update</h2>
    <p>
      Open <code>package.json</code>, <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>, or <code>pnpm-workspace.yml</code>.
      CodeLens presents applicable targets directly above supported entries.
    </p>
    <dl class="docs-reference docs-targets">
      <div><dt><code>patch</code></dt><dd>The highest available patch in the current minor version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>minor</code></dt><dd>The nearest higher minor in the current major version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>major</code></dt><dd>The nearest higher major version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>latest</code></dt><dd>The npm latest dist-tag, or the newest stable version when that tag is
        unavailable.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="hover-details">
    <h2 id="hover-details">Inspect first, then apply</h2>
    <p>
      Hover a dependency name or range to inspect its resolved and latest versions, available update targets, npm links,
      and vulnerability details. The quick-fix menu can update one dependency, all compatible dependencies,
      or all dependencies to latest in the current manifest.
    </p>
    <p>
      Catalog-backed actions edit the matching pnpm catalog entry. Major and latest updates can cross a breaking version
      boundary; review the package’s release notes and test the consuming code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="commands">
    <h2 id="commands">Keep useful commands close</h2>
    <p>Open the command palette and search for <code>Dep Beacon:</code>.</p>
    <dl class="docs-reference">
      {commands.map(command => (
        <div><dt>{command.name}</dt><dd>{command.description}</dd></div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="status-colors">
    <h2 id="status-colors">A small signal, a clear meaning</h2>
    <dl class="docs-status-list">
      <div><dt><Badge variant="success">Green · current</Badge></dt><dd>The declared range already accepts the
        latest stable version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><Badge variant="warning">Yellow · update</Badge></dt><dd>A newer target is available.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><Badge class="docs-risk-warning" variant="warning">Orange · advisory</Badge></dt><dd>OSV reports low
        or medium vulnerability risk.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><Badge variant="destructive">Red · attention</Badge></dt><dd>A package or version is invalid,
        missing, or has high or critical vulnerability risk.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <nav class="docs-next" aria-label="Related guides">
    <Link href="/docs/configuration">Adjust your settings <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
    <Link href="/docs/pnpm-workspaces">Connect a pnpm workspace <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
  </nav>
</Docs>
